                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8f3c9811-71ba-3adc-b2bb-4828b2c2b797",
                        "entry_id": "e00c0e49-1c5e-3f19-a590-c34cbe290a69",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. в светском обществе — поклон с приседанием как знак приветствия или благодарности со стороны лиц женского пола"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "55cb29ca-e7f4-44bc-88bc-434cc56aecaf",
                                "sense_id": "8f3c9811-71ba-3adc-b2bb-4828b2c2b797",
                                "text": "Девушка после того сделала прощальный книксен князю и пошла, колеблясь своим тонким станом."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "415f2e10-277a-4d5d-a2fe-e7239c38025f",
                        "source_entry_id": "e00c0e49-1c5e-3f19-a590-c34cbe290a69",
                        "source_sense_id": "8f3c9811-71ba-3adc-b2bb-4828b2c2b797",
                        "target_lang_word": "curtsey",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "curtsey",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bed31b69-4f5a-304f-920c-65cd84cb29fc",
                                        "entry_id": "1a240e8e-f4e9-355d-9d56-f77d46b6c4b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small bow, generally performed by a woman or a girl, where she crosses the shin of one leg behind the calf of her other leg and briefly bends her knees to lower her body in deference."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da8138d4-74c6-4137-b321-49a74ab4068e",
                                                "sense_id": "bed31b69-4f5a-304f-920c-65cd84cb29fc",
                                                "text": "I refused to make so much as a curtsey for the passing nobles, as I am a staunch egalitarian."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55e5b846-d0a2-4dd1-a580-469183a1239d",
                                                "sense_id": "bed31b69-4f5a-304f-920c-65cd84cb29fc",
                                                "text": "Wid. I take my leaue with many thouſand thankes. / Rich. The Match is made, ſhee ſeales it with a Curſie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ad137df-79bd-4672-9e61-d90299abd2b7",
                                                "sense_id": "bed31b69-4f5a-304f-920c-65cd84cb29fc",
                                                "text": "[I]t was her favorite amusement to array herself in the faded brocades, and parade up and down before the long mirror, making stately courtesies, and sweeping her train about, with a rustle which delighted her ears."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "247b1209-8afa-42c1-921a-358a251facdf",
                                                "sense_id": "bed31b69-4f5a-304f-920c-65cd84cb29fc",
                                                "text": "No caps were touched, no curtseys bobbed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "curtsey",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0cd37c7d-22bb-3931-aa36-dedc87f97c67",
                                        "entry_id": "1f3c5680-731b-34dd-8a11-28b164771154",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make a curtsey."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b9f5fe9-b9af-4a19-8245-1090b94b4ce5",
                                                "sense_id": "0cd37c7d-22bb-3931-aa36-dedc87f97c67",
                                                "text": "The hotel's staff never curtsied, nodded, or bowed to the owner as she passed, as they were staunch egalitarians."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bfa825d-dbab-45ff-8f1c-031895d2cd01",
                                                "sense_id": "0cd37c7d-22bb-3931-aa36-dedc87f97c67",
                                                "text": "\"I’m sure you’ll excuse me, sir,\" said Mrs Varden, rising and curtseying."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4476b519-dde4-47c6-aa1c-9bf9391e951b",
                                                "sense_id": "0cd37c7d-22bb-3931-aa36-dedc87f97c67",
                                                "text": "On the other hand, Mrs. Ladbrook was standing in skull-cap and front, with her turban in her hand, curtsying and smiling blandly[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1482045d-7caf-4828-aae5-3b86af14bf53",
                                                "sense_id": "0cd37c7d-22bb-3931-aa36-dedc87f97c67",
                                                "text": "'I be as nothing in the eyes of my lord,' and she curtseyed towards him[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee43ad1c-5586-441e-821f-c61adc9f05dd",
                                                "sense_id": "0cd37c7d-22bb-3931-aa36-dedc87f97c67",
                                                "text": "1890, James Russell Lowell, Address in Publications of the Modern Language Association of America\nBut DANTE was a great genius, and language curtseys to its natural Kings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56b58e94-c23e-4478-9364-df366b188b53",
                                                "sense_id": "0cd37c7d-22bb-3931-aa36-dedc87f97c67",
                                                "text": "1903, W.E.B. DuBois, The Souls of Black Folk\nHe curtsied low, and then bowed almost to the ground, with an imperturbable gravity that seemed almost suspicious."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "208e53aa-988e-4448-a7db-398b5f7fc85b",
                                                "sense_id": "0cd37c7d-22bb-3931-aa36-dedc87f97c67",
                                                "text": "1908, Caroline Crawford, Folk Dances and Games\nThe gentleman bows and the lady curtesys (measure eight)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "703561a5-e0f0-4ccb-b810-dc6ed97c4e60",
                        "source_entry_id": "e00c0e49-1c5e-3f19-a590-c34cbe290a69",
                        "source_sense_id": "8f3c9811-71ba-3adc-b2bb-4828b2c2b797",
                        "target_lang_word": "Knicks",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Knicks",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa8c1482-8ef1-3ba3-b675-6d0adc17c8cd",
                                        "entry_id": "8f77f79f-730a-399c-86cb-67774189f1a7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "kurze Kniebeuge eines Mädchens oder (bei Hofe) einer Dame als (veraltende) Respektbezeugung und (seltener) Grußform"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f95bc21-9ce4-4ac8-8c1f-d5c7740ae3ca",
                                                "sense_id": "aa8c1482-8ef1-3ba3-b675-6d0adc17c8cd",
                                                "text": "Sei artig, mach einen Knicks!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c870bf66-273d-4eba-a3ed-42075d139db7",
                                                "sense_id": "aa8c1482-8ef1-3ba3-b675-6d0adc17c8cd",
                                                "text": "Ein Knicks, welcher von einem Mädchen in Gegenwart der Eltern (besonders vor ihrer Mutter) ausgeführt wurde, galt lange Zeit als Zeichen der Anerkennung der elterlichen Autorität gegenüber dem Kind."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1564fb33-992a-470a-97a0-11694aa3a52d",
                                                "sense_id": "aa8c1482-8ef1-3ba3-b675-6d0adc17c8cd",
                                                "text": "In einigen Kulturen war oder ist es (noch) üblich, dass eine Dame vor oder nach einem Tanz vor ihrem Tanzpartner einen Knicks praktiziert."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4db2db18-0336-426a-a314-7d364d895301",
                                                "sense_id": "aa8c1482-8ef1-3ba3-b675-6d0adc17c8cd",
                                                "text": "„Sie machte ehrfurchtsvoll einen Knicks.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64a10528-6346-4be6-87dc-a95146fd8172",
                                                "sense_id": "aa8c1482-8ef1-3ba3-b675-6d0adc17c8cd",
                                                "text": "„Dann erscheint eine sehr gut gekleidete Frau, gefolgt von einer Magd, die Leintücher bringt und nach einem untertänigen Knicks mein Bett bezieht.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55fcf1ec-0f1c-43a8-ba60-fd774149589e",
                                                "sense_id": "aa8c1482-8ef1-3ba3-b675-6d0adc17c8cd",
                                                "text": "„Guđriđur blickt auf, lächelt, als wäre sie mit ihren Gedanken noch woanders, gedanklich so sehr mit dem Buch beschäftigt, dass die Magd, ein achtzehnjähriges Mädchen, das sich wie die anderen im Haus darauf gefreut hat, die Frau von der Hochheide zu empfangen, sie so stolz und würdevoll findet, dass sie unwillkürlich einen Knicks macht, als wäre Guđriđur eine hochgestellte Dame.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
